T781	Entity 37065 37074	Mr. Elton
T782	Cue 55675 55684	succeeded
T786	Quotation 75973 76700	"this is most strange!-- After I had got him off so well, to chuse to go into company, and leave Harriet ill behind!-- Most strange indeed!-- But there is, I believe, in many men, especially single men, such an inclination-- such a passion for dining out -- a dinner engagement is so high in the class of their pleasures, their employments, their dignities, almost their duties, that any thing gives way to it-- and this must be the case with Mr. Elton; a most valuable, amiable, pleasing young man undoubtedly, and very much in love with Harriet; but still, he cannot refuse an invitation, he must dine out wherever he is asked.  What a strange thing love is! he can see ready wit in Harriet, but will not dine alone for her."
